# Project rules

`CLAUDE.md` at the repo root is the authoritative project constitution. Follow it.
This file summarizes the rules that matter most in the editor.

## Stack

Expo SDK 57 · React Native 0.86 · React 19.2 · TypeScript strict
Expo Router (typed routes) · **NativeWind 4.2 with Tailwind v3, NOT v4**
React Native Reusables · TanStack Query · Zustand · React Hook Form + Zod
FlashList v2 · Reanimated v4 · Supabase · Stripe

## Hard rules

1. Verify any package before suggesting it: `npm view <pkg> version time.modified`
2. Expo packages install with `npx expo install`, never `pnpm add`
3. Never edit `ios/` or `android/` — generated. Use config plugins.
4. No hardcoded colors. Semantic tokens: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`
5. Import `Text` from `~/components/ui/text`, never `react-native`
6. All data-driven lists use FlashList, never `.map()` in a ScrollView
7. Auth tokens in `expo-secure-store` only
8. `{count > 0 && <X/>}` never `{count && <X/>}` — the latter renders `0` and crashes
9. Money is integer cents, never floats
10. No `any`, no `@ts-ignore` without an explanatory comment

## Architecture

- `app/` = routes only, thin screens, no business logic
- `src/features/<name>/` = api · keys · hooks · schemas · types · utils · components
- Components use hooks, never `api.ts` directly
- `components/ui/` never imports from `features/`

## Definition of done

`pnpm verify` passes · works on iOS **and** Android · loading/empty/error states ·
accessibility roles and labels · light and dark mode · safe areas.

If you can't verify a platform, say so. Don't claim it works.

## Ask first

New dependency · new `components/ui/` component · schema change or migration ·
anything touching payments, auth, or authorization · changes to `app.config.ts`.

## High-stakes code

Money, auth, RLS policies, migrations, permissions, native config: draft only, and
flag clearly for line-by-line human review. Enumerate failure modes explicitly —
concurrent access, partial failure, retry/double-submit, wrong user, malformed input.
